 lp('**A deployment plan is only credible when the people on it are ready, supported and available.** Offshore service teams need the right competencies and country-specific compliance, but they also need a leader who follows up on workload, development and wellbeing between projects. That is how the Field Operations Resource Team can support safe execution without treating people as interchangeable capacity.')
 lp('Vestas is building a sustainable energy future through wind, and this role connects that purpose to the everyday work of Service Technicians and Supervisors. The relevant foundation is practical people management and financial accountability: ELOHVAC combines leadership of five electricians and three apprentices with 1:1s, development discussions and full P&L. Ventek-Air required coordination of 14 people across 11 simultaneous projects; Novo Nordisk involved 25 specialists across 37 capital projects.')
 lp('**People, readiness, deployment.** Start with individual conversations about workload, wellbeing and development goals; combine these with service managers’ project forecasts. A shared readiness overview can show availability, required competencies, training status, expiry dates and country-specific requirements, with an owner and next action for each gap. Before deployment, authorised specialists should confirm compliance and regional Health and Safety requirements; afterwards, feedback should inform the next development discussion.')
 lp('Budget responsibility requires the same clarity: agree the cost baseline, track changes and explain variances to management and other stakeholders. ELOHVAC’s full P&L responsibility and Novo Nordisk project budgets, SAP ERP and reporting provide the relevant foundation. Cross-functional work at Novo Nordisk connected engineering, procurement and construction; I would apply that discipline to resource planning and broader Vestas projects while learning the company’s People Review, Merit, Motivation and Performance Dialogue processes.')
 lp('Offshore wind service and sustained remote management across multiple time zones are not documented in the experience presented here. The initial plan would therefore be to learn Vestas’ offshore procedures and country requirements from experienced colleagues and agree meeting times, escalation routes and written handovers suitable for a distributed team. Professional English and Danish support communication.')
 lp('I would welcome a conversation about the team’s upcoming demand, the development priorities for its technicians and the confirmed work location for requisition 75708. Vestas’ emphasis on fair hiring, collaboration and safe execution is a strong foundation for the practical people leadership this role needs.')
 m.meta('Kind regards',after=6);m.meta('Shahram Ajloo · +45 93 99 95 14 · ajlooshahram@gmail.com',after=0)
 m.page_break();m.resume_header(NAME,TITLE,CONTACT,'PROFILE — LEADERSHIP THAT PREPARES PEOPLE')
 m.para('Offshore service readiness depends on people development, safe deployment and accountable capacity planning. Relevant evidence: ELOHVAC’s eight employees, 1:1s and full P&L; Ventek-Air’s 14 people across 11 projects; Novo Nordisk’s 25 specialists across 37 capital projects. B.Tech in Technology Management and Mechanical Engineering; PRINCE2 certified. Offshore wind and long-term remote leadership across time zones are not documented experience.',after=35)
 m.section('THE READINESS CONVERSATION — MY APPROACH')
 for a,b in [('Wellbeing and development','Use regular 1:1s to understand workload and motivation; agree development goals and follow up, with attention to wellbeing and work-life balance.'),('Competence and deployment','Work with service managers and training specialists to check availability, skills and country-specific compliance before allocating people to projects.'),('Delivery and accountability','Track capacity, budget and open actions, communicate priorities across functions and follow regional health and safety requirements.')]:m.bullet(a,b,after=11)
